# --- never commit: credentials -----------------------------------------------
# The vendor sheet carries live builder portal passwords. It is READ at runtime by
# BuilderRegistry and at build time by api/_export_builders.py (which strips the
# credential columns before anything is deployed), so the file stays on disk — it just
# must never be in the repo. It WAS committed from the initial commit and is already
# public on GitHub; removing it here stops further exposure but does not undo that, so
# those passwords need rotating.
Book1(Builders) List.csv
*Builders* List.csv
drive_input/
.sessions/
.env
credentials.json

